    "summary": "Both gaps closed. Startup: src/daemon/index.ts now imports registerParkOffer and main() calls it right after installStepDaemonClient(...) before the IPC server starts (stepToolTable keeps its idempotent call too), and a new test in park-offer.test.ts checks that wiring in main(). Terminal: the CLI runs the gate in its own process with no run store, so makeServices() in src/cli/services/index.ts registers a provider there that offers on an uncommitted draft only: handoff.ts gains draftParkOffer(repo, unit) (unitDraftFiles non-empty for an Epic or Story unit, never throws), which the daemon's hasUnparkedWork also uses for its draft half. The named integration test now also drives the real terminal command: with bob holding the Story and no draft, 'team claim <hash> s1' prints exactly '✗ not claimed — held by bob'; after an untracked LLD.md appears in the Story's folder it prints '✗ not claimed — held by bob; ... team park <epicHash> [storyId]'. Everything else in that test (owned run in each stage, case-insensitive owner, no meta / empty meta / another owner / another story / another repo / non-claim-unit workflow giving false, untracked, committed, modified and markdown drafts, the workflow-step refusal text with and without an offer) is unchanged and passes. park-offer.test.ts has 3 passing tests; team suite 81 and cli 207 pass (the cli poll-interval flake aside); tsc clean.",
